This will just add bloat rather than help. Honestly, the functionality is working so this is just over-engineering. Let me explain the problem I am seeing in the current code. Down below I have shown the 2 worst case scenarios for this
```js
FormData {
  "obj.some.thing": "1",
  "obj.some.thing": "1",
  "obj.some.thing": "1",
}

// OR

FormData {
  "obj.some.thing": "1",
  "obj.some.one": "1",
  "obj.some.hello": "1",
}
```

Both cases have a complexity of **O(mn)** where _m_ is the number of entries and _n_ is the number of subkeys in an entry. We can improve this to **O(m+n)** simply by changing the loop of `convertFormDataToBodyData` and minor changes in the `handleParsingNestedValues` function. Here are the changes respectively -

We are just processing the values separately. This first put the data in arrays the same as the old code and then converts it into a nested structure if the dot prop is `true`, only to the ones who have a `.`.
```ts
const form: BodyData = Object.create(null)

formData.forEach((value, key) => {
  const shouldParseAllValues = options.all || key.endsWith('[]')

  if (shouldParseAllValues) {
    handleParsingAllValues(form, key, value)
  } else {
    form[key] = value
  }
})

if (options.dot) {
  const nestedForm: BodyData = Object.create(null)

  Object.entries(form).forEach(([key, value]) => {
    const shouldParseDotValues = key.includes('.')

    if (shouldParseDotValues) {
      handleParsingNestedValues(nestedForm, key, value)
    } else {
      nestedForm[key] = value
    }
  })

  return nestedForm as T
}

return form as T
```
And remove the `parseAllValues` param as we don't need it now.
```ts
const handleParsingNestedValues = (
  form: BodyData,
  key: string,
  value: BodyDataValue
): void => {
  let nestedForm = form
  const keys = key.split('.')

  keys.forEach((key, index) => {
    if (index === keys.length - 1) {
        nestedForm[key] = value
    } else {
      if (
        !nestedForm[key] ||
        typeof nestedForm[key] !== 'object' ||
        Array.isArray(nestedForm[key]) ||
        nestedForm[key] instanceof File
      ) {
        nestedForm[key] = Object.create(null)
      }
      nestedForm = nestedForm[key] as BodyData
    }
  })
}
```
Overall this will improve the simplicity of the code and also the complexity. We can further improve the complexity of this but as I said before it's just over-engineering. Until @yusukebe wants us to improve this further we are good.

